1. Start Qdrant (Database)
Open terminal 1:

powershell


cd "C:\Users\Lenovo\Desktop\SearchEngine(Main)\HoloSearchEngine"
docker-compose up -d
2. Start the Embedding Service
Open terminal 2:

powershell


cd "C:\Users\Lenovo\Desktop\SearchEngine(Main)\HoloSearchEngine"
.\venv\Scripts\activate
cd embeded_service
uvicorn main:app --port 8000
3. Start the AI Summary Service
Open terminal 3:

powershell


cd "C:\Users\Lenovo\Desktop\SearchEngine(Main)\HoloSearchEngine"
.\venv\Scripts\activate
# Make sure your API key is exported so it doesn't get disabled
$env:GEMINI_API_KEY="YOUR_GOOGLE_STUDIO_API_KEY"
cd ai_summary
uvicorn main:app --port 8001
4. Start the Rust API
Open terminal 4:

powershell


cd "C:\Users\Lenovo\Desktop\SearchEngine(Main)\HoloSearchEngine\api"
$env:TANTIVY_PATH="../tantivy_index"
$env:EMBEDDING_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8000"
$env:QDRANT_URL="http://127.0.0.1:6333"
$env:AI_SUMMARY_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8001"
cargo run
5. Start the Next.js Frontend
Open terminal 5:

powershell


cd "C:\Users\Lenovo\Desktop\SearchEngine(Main)\HoloSearchEngine\frontend\holo-search-engine"
$env:NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8080"
npm run dev
Go to http://localhost:3000
 in your browser, search for "One Piece", and let's see if those new "Watch on Crunchyroll" / "Watch on Netflix" buttons appear on the search card!